@SceneEats: West Cairo matcha drinkers, your Matter fix is moving closer to home. Matter, Cairo’s matcha house known for converting coffee loyalists, is opening a new location at Arkan in Sheikh Zayed, bringing its green brews a little closer to the neighbourhood.

Matter has built its following around a matcha-led menu that puts a fresh spin on the daily caffeine run. Founded by Reem Hassan, a former professional coffee taster, the brand approaches matcha with the same attention to ingredients and preparation as specialty coffee, serving classic lattes alongside more experimental blends.

For more snackable content from across Egypt, head to www.SceneEats.com (link in bio) or download the SceneNow app.

@SceneEats: New Cairo has a new coffee stop, and this one comes straight from Colombia. Juan Valdez, the Colombian coffee chain known for its 100% Colombian coffee, has officially opened at Park St. East.

The menu centres on Colombian coffee, with brewed classics alongside drinks like the Arequipe Cappuccino, a caramel-forward option for those who prefer their coffee on the sweeter side, and Matcha Nevados for anyone looking to switch up their usual order.

